{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The trip record carries a driver 'arrived' event for this trip: 'Driver tapped I'm Here' at 2026-08-18T21:26:22+08:00, which satisfies limb (a) of POL-NS-01 on the face of the record.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-02728"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.events[event_type=driver_arrived].at",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Limb (b) of POL-NS-01 is met on the GPS trace: the driver's longest qualifying run inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius begins at 2026-08-18T21:26:22+08:00 — the exact timestamp of the arrival event — so the driver was inside the pickup geofence at or before that event. The run contains 45 qualifying fixes and the driver's minimum recorded distance from the pin is 0.11 m, far inside the radius.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02728", "EV-TRIP-02728"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01", "POL-NS-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.longest_qualifying_run.first_ts",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Limb (c) of POL-NS-01 is met with a wide margin: the driver held position inside the geofence for a continuous 436 seconds — 45 qualifying fixes from 21:26:22 to 21:33:38 — against the free waiting period of 180 seconds in force for this trip under trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec. The dwell does not need to be reconstructed from the arrival tap, because it is measured from the first qualifying in-geofence fix, and here the two coincide.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02728", "EV-TRIP-02728"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.longest_qualifying_run.duration_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Limb (d) of POL-NS-01 is met: the trip record shows no boarding event, and the trip was terminated by the driver at 21:33:39 under cancellation_reason_code RIDER_NO_SHOW — one second after the 436 second in-geofence dwell completed at 21:33:38, and 436 seconds after that dwell began. The cancellation therefore falls after the required dwell elapsed and under a reason code POL-NS-01(d) recognises.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-02728", "EV-GPS-02728"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.cancellation_reason_code",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The false-arrival check in POL-NS-05 does not bite on this trip. The arrival marker carries a dwell_start_offset_sec of 0.0, meaning the first qualifying in-geofence fix is contemporaneous with the 'arrived' tap, so the marker neither post-dates the geofence entry nor depends on a recomputed clock. Even if the marker were treated as false, POL-NS-05(iii) preserves the fee where the corrected dwell still meets the minimum — and 436 seconds does.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02728", "EV-TRIP-02728"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-05"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.dwell_start_offset_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No waiting-period shortfall exists under POL-NS-06: the measured in-geofence dwell exceeds the 180 second minimum by 256 seconds (shortfall_sec = -256.0), so the cancellation fee is chargeable and no refund route in that clause opens.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02728"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-06"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.shortfall_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-NS-04 cannot exonerate the rider on this record. Limb (a) fails because the chat log contains exactly one message and it was sent by the driver, not the rider. Limb (c) fails affirmatively on admissible fixes: there are zero qualifying rider fixes (rider_qualifying_fix_count = 0) and the rider's device sat between 797.9 m and 804.8 m from the pickup pin throughout — roughly eight times the 100 m STANDARD rider presence radius.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-02728", "EV-GPS-02728"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-04"],
      "relies_on": "derived.rider_presence.min_distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The chat log corroborates the driver's account: at 21:26:42, within twenty seconds of the arrival marker, the driver wrote 'im at the pickup point', delivered at 21:26:43 and read by the rider at 21:27:12. The rider never replied before the driver terminated the trip at 21:33:39, and the counterparty statement on file says 'Rider did not show after the waiting period.' The driver did everything the no-show process asks of him.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-02728", "EV-TRIP-02728"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "chat_log.messages[0].sent_at",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-NS-03 does not apply and yields no refund route. That clause governs stationary fixes OUTSIDE the arrival radius but within 400 m of the pin; here the driver's stationary fixes are inside the 50 m STANDARD radius (minimum distance 0.11 m), so the wrong-entrance band is never entered. Independently, registered_pickup_points is 1, so the pin-ambiguity goodwill of POL-NS-03(ii) — which requires 2 or more registered points — could not arise on these facts either.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02728", "EV-TRIP-02728"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-03"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.registered_pickup_points",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The POL-NS-07 anti-farming check does not trip, so compensation is paid rather than withheld. It requires BOTH limbs: no_show_terminations_30d of 4 or more AND that count divided by completed_trips_30d greater than 0.08. The driver's trailing-30-day no-show terminations stand at 3 (below 4) and 3 divided by 40 completed trips is 0.075 (not greater than 0.08). This is the only profile test the clause permits, and it is passed.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-02728"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-07"],
      "relies_on": "driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's payout is SGD 3.60 — 80 percent of the SGD 4.50 cancellation fee in force for this trip, with the residual 20 percent retained as the platform service fee. That is the net figure the platform's own money block computes from POL-NS-07 (driver_compensation '3.60'), and it is deliberately not the rider's gross figure of SGD 6.61.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02728", "EV-TRIP-02728"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-07"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.driver_compensation",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The ruling on this case is DRIVER_COMPENSATION, not a bare NO_ACTION. POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full on limbs (a) through (d), no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces it, and POL-NS-07 therefore fixes the driver's payout and requires the emitted ruling value to be DRIVER_COMPENSATION with amount_sgd mirroring driver_compensation_sgd. The rider's charge of SGD 4.50 stands as it presently is (payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00) with no refund.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02728", "EV-TRIP-02728"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-07", "POL-GEN-03"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.payment_status",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No escalation trigger under POL-NS-09 is engaged. Counterparty dispute history is zero on both sides, so limb (c) cannot fire; the rider's no_show_disputes_30d is 0, so limb (d) cannot fire; the POL-NS-07 anti-farming check does not trip, so the other half of limb (d) cannot fire; and there is no direct contradiction between artifacts, since the platform's arrival event and the GPS first in-geofence fix agree to the second and the fare line reconciles exactly to the net fee. The automated pipeline can decide this case.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-RPROF-02728", "EV-DPROF-02728", "EV-FARE-02728", "EV-TRIP-02728"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-09"],
      "relies_on": "rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Nothing in this bundle is impaired, so no claim of mine is discounted. Every artifact is COMPLETE at weight 1.0: the GPS trace has 100.0 percent coverage, a 10 second cadence, an empty gaps list and a max_gap_sec of 0.0, so POL-NS-08(b) is not engaged; the chat log's single message matches the trip record's chat_message_count of 1 and its msg_id sequence is intact, so POL-NS-08(c) is not engaged; and the fare_breakdown cancellation-fee line of 4.50 equals the net amount produced for this trip, so POL-NS-08(d) is not engaged. The arrival event matched to a GPS fix carries no clock skew beyond 90 seconds — it matches to the second.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02728", "EV-CHAT-02728", "EV-FARE-02728", "EV-TRIP-02728"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-08", "POL-GEN-02"],
      "relies_on": "admissibility.weight_multiplier",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The one MISSING artifact, the traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-02728-01, is disclosed as impaired: it carries status MISSING, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT and weight_multiplier 0.0, and its payload is absent. The driver does not rely on it, and does not need to: the advisory matters only to POL-NS-06(i), which permits separated in-geofence intervals to be summed. Here there is a single unbroken 436 second run inside the radius (run_count = 1), so no accumulation and no advisory is required. The absence is citable but neutral — it neither excuses a shortfall nor creates one.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-02728-01", "EV-GPS-02728"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-06", "POL-GEN-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.accumulated_dwell.run_count",
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "For completeness on the money: the waiting-time line on this trip is 0.00, so nothing was double-charged, and the only amount on the ledger is the 4.50 cancellation fee that POL-NS-01 makes chargeable and POL-NS-07 splits 80/20 in the driver's favour. The rider's $4.50 was the consideration for a driver who arrived, waited 436 seconds and messaged the rider; it is not refundable and it is not the platform's to keep alone.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02728"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-10", "POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.waiting_time_fee",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "DRIVER_COMPENSATION",
    "amount_sgd": 3.6,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": 3.6,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "This one is decided for the driver on the platform's own records, so both of you should read why.\n\nDriver: you tapped 'I'm Here' at 21:26:22 on 18 Aug. The GPS trace puts your device inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius from that very second — your closest fix is 0.11 m from the pickup pin — and shows you holding position there without a break from 21:26:22 to 21:33:38: a single continuous 436-second dwell across 45 qualifying fixes. The free waiting period in force for this trip is 180 seconds (trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec), so you waited 256 seconds beyond the minimum before cancelling at 21:33:39 under reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW, with no boarding event. All four conditions of POL-NS-01 are met.\n\nRider: none of the refund routes helps on these facts, and your own advocate did not press them. POL-NS-06 does not apply because there is no shortfall — the dwell exceeds the 180-second minimum, it does not fall short. POL-NS-05 does not apply because the arrival marker is not false: the derived dwell start offset is 0.0 seconds, meaning the first qualifying in-geofence fix and the arrival tap are the same moment. POL-NS-04 does not apply because the only message in the chat log was sent by the driver ('im at the pickup point', 21:26:42), so there was no unanswered rider contact, and in any event your track shows your device roughly 798–805 m from the pin for the whole window, far outside the 100 m rider presence radius. POL-NS-03 does not apply because the driver's stationary fixes are inside the arrival radius, not in the 400 m wrong-entrance band.\n\nMoney. The cancelled amount is SGD 4.50, which is the fee in force for this trip (trip_record.platform_policy.cancellation_fee_sgd) and the amount on the fare ledger (payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00). It stands; the rider is not refunded. Under POL-NS-07 the driver receives 80 per cent of that fee, SGD 3.60, with the residual 20 per cent retained as the platform service fee. The anti-farming check does not trip: trailing-30-day no-show terminations are 3 (the test needs 4 or more) and 3 divided by 40 completed trips is 0.075 (the test needs more than 0.08). Because a driver payment is made, the ruling value is DRIVER_COMPENSATION, and per POL-GEN-03 amount_sgd carries the same SGD 3.60 figure as driver_compensation_sgd — it is the amount the ruling moves, not a second payment and not a refund to the rider.\n\nEvidence disclosure. EV-ADVIS-02728-01 (traffic advisory) is MISSING, weight 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT. It is named here because it sits in the bundle, but it carries no deciding fact: the driver's dwell is one unbroken in-geofence run, so POL-NS-06(i)'s permission to sum separate intervals — the only thing an advisory bears on — is never needed, and its absence neither supports nor caps anything. Every artifact that does carry a deciding fact (the GPS trace, trip record, fare breakdown and driver profile) is COMPLETE at weight 1.0, and the two sides' accounts agree with the instruments, so nothing is discounted and confidence is not capped below 1.0. No clause of the policy produces a referral on these facts, so the referrals list is empty. The monetary effect, SGD 3.60, is below the SGD 8.00 automatic execution threshold, so it executes on issue; both parties retain the appeal route under POL-GEN-04."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "DRIVER_COMPENSATION",
    "amount_sgd": 3.60,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": 3.60,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.94,
    "explanation": "Both parties agree on the arithmetic, and the record supports them. POL-NS-01 is satisfied on all four limbs. (a) The trip record carries the driver's 'arrived' event at 21:26:22. (b) The GPS trace puts his first qualifying in-geofence fix at the same second — dwell_start_offset_sec 0.0 — with a minimum recorded distance from the pin of 0.11 m, well inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius. (c) He then held position for a single unbroken run of 436 seconds (45 consecutive in-radius fixes, 21:26:22 to 21:33:38) against the free waiting period of 180 s carried in trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec; no_show_threshold_sec is null, so no longer threshold applies. (d) There is no boarding event, and the trip was terminated by the driver at 21:33:39 under RIDER_NO_SHOW — one second after the required dwell elapsed, under a reason code limb (d) recognises. The record's reason code is not mis-selected and no false-arrival or driver-education referral arises.\n\nEvery refund route fails on this record, and both advocates say so. POL-NS-06: the dwell exceeds the minimum by 256 s (shortfall_sec -256.0), so there is no shortfall to refund. POL-NS-05: the arrival marker coincides with geofence entry at a standing speed, so it is not a false marker; POL-NS-05(ii) is not engaged and no false-arrival referral is recorded. POL-NS-03: the driver's stationary fixes are inside the arrival radius, so the wrong-entrance band (outside the radius, within 400 m) is never entered, and registered_pickup_points is 1, so pin-ambiguity goodwill cannot arise either. POL-NS-04: the chat log's single message was sent by the driver ('im at the pickup point', 21:26:42, read 21:27:12), not the rider, so limb (a) fails; and the rider's own track shows 0 qualifying fixes at roughly 798–805 m from the pin, so limb (c) fails affirmatively as well. The rider's distance from the pin is not an element of the charge — POL-NS-01 does not test rider position — and I record it as context only, not as a separate adverse finding. The rider's point that the driver's position-holding needs no traffic advisory is correct: the dwell is one unbroken run (run_count 1), so POL-NS-06(i) accumulation is neither needed nor available.\n\nPOL-NS-07 therefore fixes the payout. The cancellation fee in force for this trip is SGD 4.50 (trip_record.platform_policy.cancellation_fee_sgd, reconciling to the fare_breakdown line of 4.50); driver compensation is 80 percent of that net figure = SGD 3.60, with SGD 0.90 (20 percent) retained as the platform service fee. The anti-farming check is passed on its two required limbs: no_show_terminations_30d is 3 (below 4) and 3 divided by 40 completed trips is 0.075 (not greater than 0.08) — no other profile field is used for that test. Compensation is therefore paid, not withheld, and no POL-NS-09 escalation is engaged: confidence is above the 0.70 floor, no admissible artifacts contradict each other on arrival, dwell or rider presence, counterparty dispute history is 0 on both sides, the rider's no_show_disputes_30d is 0, and no deciding fact rests on an impaired artifact. The rider's SGD 4.50 charge stands as it presently is (payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00) with no refund. Per POL-GEN-03, amount_sgd mirrors driver_compensation_sgd at SGD 3.60 on this ruling value.\n\nConfidence 0.94. The deciding facts are carried by EV-TRIP-02728 and EV-GPS-02728, both COMPLETE at weight_multiplier 1.0, and the trace's 100.0 percent coverage, 10 s cadence and empty gaps list (max_gap_sec 0.0) engage no limb of POL-NS-08(a)–(d). EV-ADVIS-02728-01 is MISSING, weight 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, and its payload is absent; its absence is disclosed and citable but neutral here, because the driver's case rests on a single unbroken in-geofence run and needs no traffic advisory. The monetary effect is SGD 3.60, below the SGD 8.00 execution threshold, so the ruling executes on issue. Both parties may appeal under POL-GEN-04."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
